@baseUrl = http://localhost:5280
@mailboxId = 50a1bff5-7bc4-4da0-824e-07ac4014571f
@mailboxAddress = tobys@6w020f.onmicrosoft.com
@messageId = REPLACE-WITH-GRAPH-MESSAGE-ID
@subscriptionId = REPLACE-WITH-GRAPH-SUBSCRIPTION-ID

###
# ─── IGraphSubscriptionClient ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Every request here calls live Microsoft Graph. Creating a subscription additionally requires
# Graph to be able to REACH Graph:Subscription:NotificationBaseUrl — see README.md.
###

### IGraphSubscriptionClient.SubscribeAsync
### Expect 200 with { id, resourceId, changeTypes, expiresAt }. changeTypes reflects the configured
### Graph:Subscription:ChangeTypes, and resource is ResourceTemplate with {resourceId} substituted.
### Copy the returned id into @subscriptionId above. Graph rejects the call if it cannot validate
### the notificationUrl, which surfaces as a 500.
POST {{baseUrl}}/graph/subscriptions/{{mailboxId}}

###

### IGraphSubscriptionClient.GetActiveSubscribedResourceIdsAsync
### Expect 200 with the raw resource-path segment of every active subscription. Segments are
### returned unnormalized — a subscription created before an identifier migration comes back as its
### address, not an id.
GET {{baseUrl}}/graph/subscriptions/active

###

### IGraphSubscriptionClient.GetActiveSubscribedResourceIdsAsync (filtered by change type)
### Expect 200 with only those subscriptions whose changeType overlaps the requested flags.
### Omitting changeTypes (the request above) means None, which applies no filtering at all.
GET {{baseUrl}}/graph/subscriptions/active?changeTypes=Created

###

### IGraphSubscriptionClient.GetSubscriptionByIdAsync
### Expect 200 with the subscription, or 200 with a null body if Graph 404s that id.
GET {{baseUrl}}/graph/subscriptions/by-id/{{subscriptionId}}

###

### IGraphSubscriptionClient.GetSubscriptionByResourceIdAsync
### Matches on the resource path's second segment, case-insensitively. Expect 200 with the
### subscription, or a null body when nothing matches.
GET {{baseUrl}}/graph/subscriptions/by-resource/{{mailboxId}}

###

### IGraphSubscriptionClient.GetSubscriptionByResourceIdentifiersAsync (transitional overload)
### Passes TWO identifiers — the current id and the legacy address form. Expect 200 with the
### subscription when EITHER matches. This is the migration path: a subscription created against
### the address is found here but NOT by the id-only request above.
GET {{baseUrl}}/graph/subscriptions/by-identifiers?identifiers={{mailboxId}},{{mailboxAddress}}

###

### IGraphSubscriptionClient.RenewSubscriptionAsync
### Issues an HTTP PATCH. Expect 200 with { "expiresAt": "<new expiry>" }, extended by the
### configured LifespanMinutes.
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/graph/subscriptions/{{subscriptionId}}

###

### IGraphSubscriptionClient.UnsubscribeAsync
### Expect 204 No Content. A 404 from Graph (subscription already gone) is tolerated and still
### returns 204; any other failure status surfaces as a 500.
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/graph/subscriptions/{{subscriptionId}}

###
